---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import club from "../data/club.json";

const lastUpdated = "9 May 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Bellshill Curling Club collects, uses and protects your personal data and member information under UK GDPR."
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 prose prose-slate">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-stone mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      {club.name} ("we", "us", "the Club") is committed to protecting your privacy.
      This page explains what information we collect when you visit this website or
      contact us, how it is used, and your rights under the UK General Data Protection
      Regulation (UK GDPR) and the Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations
      (PECR).
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      {club.name} is an amateur curling club based at {club.rink},
      {club.address}. For any privacy queries, please use our
      <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>This website does not use cookies.</strong> No tracking, advertising,
      or preference cookies are stored on your device by us. For that reason, you
      will not see a cookie consent banner.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact form</h2>
    <p>
      If you use the contact form on our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>,
      the information you submit (your name, email address, and message) is sent
      to us via <a
        href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        target="_blank">Formspree</a
      >, our form-handling provider, and forwarded to the Club's email address.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Lawful basis:</strong> your consent (UK GDPR Art. 6(1)(a)) when you
        submit the form, and our legitimate interest in responding to enquiries.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Purpose:</strong> to reply to your enquiry about membership, events,
        or other Club matters.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Retention:</strong> we keep enquiry emails only for as long as needed
        to deal with your request, and routinely delete old correspondence.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sharing:</strong> we do not sell or share your information with third
        parties for marketing.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Spam protection (Cloudflare Turnstile)</h2>
    <p>
      To stop automated spam submissions, our contact form uses
      <a
        href="https://www.cloudflare.com/products/turnstile/"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        target="_blank">Cloudflare Turnstile</a
      >, a privacy-friendly alternative to CAPTCHA. When you visit the contact
      page, Turnstile loads a small challenge in your browser to check that you
      are a real person. Turnstile:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>does not use tracking cookies;</li>
      <li>does not require you to solve image puzzles;</li>
      <li>
        processes limited technical signals (such as your IP address, browser
        type and interaction data) solely to distinguish humans from bots;
      </li>
      <li>
        is operated by Cloudflare, Inc. under their <a
          href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">privacy policy</a
        >.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This processing is necessary for our legitimate interest in preventing
      spam and abuse of the contact form.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      This website is hosted on Microsoft Azure Static Web Apps. Standard web
      server logs (such as IP address, browser user agent, and request time) may
      be processed by the hosting provider for security and reliability
      purposes. These logs are not used by the Club for tracking or marketing.
    </p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>
      Our site links to external websites (for example our Facebook page). Those
      sites have their own privacy policies and we are not responsible for their
      content or practices.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under UK GDPR you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>request a copy of any personal data we hold about you;</li>
      <li>ask us to correct inaccurate data;</li>
      <li>ask us to delete data we no longer need;</li>
      <li>object to or restrict our processing of your data;</li>
      <li>
        withdraw consent at any time (where consent is the basis for
        processing).
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these rights, please get in touch via our
      <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. You also have the right to lodge a
      complaint with the UK Information Commissioner's Office (<a
        href="https://ico.org.uk/"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        target="_blank">ico.org.uk</a
      >).
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. The "last updated" date at
      the top of the page will reflect the most recent revision.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
